<title>RUSSIA: Russian Jan automobile output rises 30 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Russian Jan automobile output rises 30 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia produced 70,100 automobiles in January, a rise of 30 percent on a year earlier, State Statistics Committee figures showed on Monday.</p>
<p>Output for all vehicles in January rose 22 percent on a year ago and fell 10 percent from December.</p>
<p>    RUSSIAN VEHICLE OUTPUT	    Jan'97   Dec '96   Jan '96</p>
<p>    total production automobiles    70,100     n/a     54,000</p>
<p>    mth/mth pct change autos		-7	+4	  -13</p>
<p>    yr/yr pct change			 +30     +22	   -8</p>
<p>    total production trucks	    9,800     n/a	  n/a</p>
<p>    mth/mth pct change trucks	    -26	+0.8	-17</p>
<p>    yr/yr pct change			 -19	+5	   +3</p>
<p>    total production buses	     3,100     n/a	2,800</p>
<p>    mth/mth pct change buses		-3     +12	  -17</p>
<p>    yr/yr pct change			 +10	-6	  -25</p>
<p>--Peter Henderson, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
